    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0FE17D4AFBB66F4F196ABBBA1DF3DF85/jobs/250985": {
      "title": "Part-Time Head Cheerleading Coach",
      "description": "Part-Time Head Cheerleading Coach You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part-Time Head Cheerleading Coach Albertus Magnus College - NEW HAVEN, CT 06511 Apply Apply Description Albertus Magnus College Position Title: Part-Time Head Cheerleading Coach Reporting To: Director of Athletics About Albertus Magnus College: Albertus Magnus College thrives as a diverse and dynamic institution serving 1,500 students in three distinct degree programs: traditional undergraduate accelerated adult undergraduate, and master’s degrees. Through its liberal arts and professional educational offerings and its long-standing excellence in student-centered, values-based education, Albertus Magnus College is a shining example of modern-day education. Explore more about the college here . Job Overview: The Head Cheerleading Coach is expected to direct the day-to-day operation and development of the program at Albertus Magnus College. The Head Coach is accountable for building the requisite roster size and developing a student-athlete recruitment plan to ensure the long-term sustainability and competitiveness of an appropriate roster. The Head Coach implements a strength and conditioning program and plans for and manages practices and games. The Head Coach also must provide positive guidance to each student-athlete that fosters and develops the premise that athletics are an integral component of the student experience and that athletic achievement must not come at the expense of academic success. Along with coaching responsibilities, this position has additional duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Qualifications Major Duties and Responsibilities : Develops and implements a recruiting plan to achieve and maintain a roster size adequate for sponsorship of Cheerleading in accordance with the College’s enrollment growth strategies. Develops and implements a practice plan to insure proper preparation for competition. Promotes the visions and values of Albertus Magnus College by emphasizing the experience and education of each student-athlete as the most important component of intercollegiate athletic participation. Supervises assistant coaches and provides feedback for continued growth and development. Represented their respective program during coaches’ meetings. Provides a year-round strength and conditioning program tailored towards the individual sport. Coordinates fundraising activities to benefit the student-athlete experience for the cheerleading program. Qualifications : Knowledge of collegiate rules and a demonstrated compliance with said rules. Outstanding verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience as a student-athlete or coach of the sport(s). General understanding of the recruiting process at the college level. A demonstrated commitment to the NCAA Division III philosophy regarding the student-athlete experience. Current safety certifications (CPR/First Aid, a valid drivers license) are required, or an ability to obtain. Education : Bachelor’s degree required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities : Outstanding verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience as a student-athlete or coach of the sport(s). General understanding of the recruiting process at the college level. A demonstrated commitment to the NCAA Division III philosophy regarding the student-athlete experience. Special Working Conditions : Evening and some weekend hours required. Work Schedule Requirements : Special Work Schedule Requirements : This position includes weekend and evening hours. Albertus Magnus College is strongly committed to the principles and practices of diversity throughout the College community. Albertus Magnus College is an equal-opportunity employer and invites all qualified applicants to consider this opportunity and apply. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0FE17D4AFBB66F4F196ABBBA1DF3DF85/jobs/252009": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Director of Financial Aid You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Financial Aid Albertus Magnus College - NEW HAVEN, CT 06511 Apply Apply Description ALBERTUS MAGNUS COLLEGE Director of Financial Aid Department Financial Aid Reports to Vice President for Enrollment Management Employment status Full-Time FLSA status Exempt Why Albertus Magnus College Founded in 1925, Albertus Magnus College has thrived through the dedication of individuals across academic and administrative roles, all committed to advancing the College’s mission and upholding the four pillars of the Dominican Tradition: Study, Prayer, Community, and Service. Today, Albertus Magnus stands as a vibrant example of modern higher education. Position Summary The Director of Financial Aid provides strategic and student-centered leadership in the Office of Financial Aid. This key position provides oversight for all financial aid operations, ensuring compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations while delivering high-quality service to students. The Director is a critical member of the Enrollment Management leadership team. The Director develops effective processes, supports a collaborative team environment, and promotes access to financial resources that help students achieve their educational goals. The Director reports to the Vice President for Enrollment Management. Qualifications Essential Duties and Responsibilities Direct and oversee all aspects of the financial aid office operations Work closely with financial aid staff to establish goals and procedures to ensure compliance in all aspects of financial aid processing Prepare and maintain annual financial aid budgets, implement packaging and awarding policies consistent with meeting the College’s enrollment, discount rate and net tuition revenue goals Responsible for updating and maintaining the College’s PPA/ECAR with the Department of Education Coordinate the processing and completion of the FISAP, CT State Grant, IPEDS, NCAA reports, and all other external and College reporting requests Responsible for responding to all borrower defense cases Administer federal, state, and institutional aid in accordance with federal, state, and institutional polices and compliance guidelines Ensure confidentiality and storage of student records according to federal, state and institutional guidelines Initiates and performs the annual setup/update of systems for financial aid processing Work collaboratively with other offices of the College including Traditional Undergraduate Admissions, Professional and Graduate Studies, Athletics, Enrollment Management Operations, Business Office, Academic Affairs and Finance offices Develops and manages communications with prospective and current students and their families Work with Finance Office on internal, state, and federal audits Develop, maintain and update financial aid consumer information for the College Manage awarding of all students Serve as liaison between the Financial Aid Office and the Athletic Department Counsel students and families on all aspects of financial aid and assist with overflow processing Serve at various campus events, financial aid presentations on and off campus, and serve on institutional committees as assigned Maintain proficient knowledge of all aspects of financial aid regulations and industry practices Supervises, trains, and evaluates Financial Aid staff Complete all R2T4s Final review for all professional judgment appeals Review and make decisions regarding SAP appeals Required Qualifications Qualifications : Ability to multi-task in a high-pressure environment Good organizational and time management skills Excellent oral and written communication skills Ability to motivate and maintain a successful team Strong people skills Education : Bachelor’s Degree Required (Master’s Degree preferred) Experience : 5-7 years of experience of increasing responsibility in Financial Aid at an accredited higher education institution Experience managing and maintaining budgets Supervisory experience Experience with enrollment management Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Technical proficiency with Excel and Microsoft Office Suite Working knowledge of various federal and state financial aid compliance rules and regulations Knowledge of PowerFAIDS, Slate, Navigate, Datatel Colleague System, ELM, or DHS SAVE System preferred Experience working with traditional and non-traditional college students and their families Knowledge of Title IV systems (i.e. COD, NSLDS, CPS, etc.) Experience developing and maintaining procedure manuals Familiarity with Single Compliance Audits Work Schedule and Flexibility Regular schedule: Work hours are typically Monday to Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Some late evenings and weekends are required for recruitment events and other college related activities. Hybrid eligibility: Yes. If eligible, hybrid work may be considered after 90 days, subject to position requirements, supervisor approval, and College policy. Benefits and Work-Life Highlights COMPENSATION Wage/Salary Range: $85,000-$105,000 annually The range shown is the College's good-faith wage range for this position. The final offer will be based on relevant experience, education, skills, internal equity, and budget considerations. For eligible full-time employees, the College offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support health, financial well-being, time away, and continued learning. HEALTH & WELL-BEING Medical, dental, and vision coverage starting the 1 st of the month following DOH. Employee wellness events and activities throughout the year TIME AWAY & FLEXIBILITY 18-23 days of paid time off annually, based on eligibility and service. Carry over unused time into the next fiscal year. 14 paid holidays plus a paid holiday break between Christmas and New Year's. Summer Fridays off from June through August, based on the College's annual summer schedule EDUCATION & RETIREMENT 100% tuition remission after 90 days for eligible employees and dependents; exclusions apply Retirement plan participation upon hire. Benefits are subject to eligibility requirements and the terms of applicable plan documents and College policies. Application Instructions Submit the following through [application portal/link]: Cover letter Resume or curriculum vitae Applicants selected for the first round of interviews will be contacted directly by the search committee or Human Resources. Albertus Magnus College is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from qualified individuals. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0FE17D4AFBB66F4F196ABBBA1DF3DF85/jobs/253172": {
      "title": "Position Summary",
      "description": "Part-Time Nursing Faculty, BSN Program You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Part-Time Nursing Faculty, BSN Program Albertus Magnus College - NEW HAVEN, CT 06511 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Apply Description ALBERTUS MAGNUS COLLEGE Part-Time Nursing Faculty, BSN Programs - Ongoing Recruitment Department Nursing Reports to Cynthia Jeffrey Employment status Temporary FLSA status To be determined by Human Resources Why Albertus Magnus College Founded in 1925, Albertus Magnus College has thrived through the dedication of individuals across academic and administrative roles, all committed to advancing the College’s mission and upholding the four pillars of the Dominican Tradition: Study, Prayer, Community, and Service. Today, Albertus Magnus stands as a vibrant example of modern higher education. Position Summary Albertus Magnus College is inviting applications for part-time nursing faculty to support the traditional BSN and LPN-to-BSN programs. Instructional opportunities may include classroom, clinical, skills laboratory, and simulation-based teaching, depending on program needs and the qualifications of the applicant. This is an ongoing recruitment process; qualified candidates will be reviewed on a rolling basis and contacted as instructional needs arise. Qualifications Essential Duties and Responsibilities Provide classroom, clinical, skills laboratory, and/or simulation instruction within the BSN and LPN-to-BSN programs, as appropriate to the faculty member's qualifications and program needs. Collaborate with course and program faculty to support student learning and achievement of course and program outcomes. Evaluate student learning, skills competency, written assignments, and/or clinical performance as appropriate to the instructional assignment. Provide timely feedback and maintain required student and course documentation. Maintain a safe, supportive, and professional learning environment and serve as a liaison to clinical agencies when assigned to clinical instruction. Meet the responsibilities of the assigned course or clinical experience in accordance with Nursing Department and College expectations. Required Qualifications For BSN and LPN-to-BSN classroom, clinical, laboratory, or simulation instruction: Registered Nurse with a current, unencumbered Connecticut RN license and a Master's degree in Nursing (MSN). Current clinical experience relevant to the instructional assignment and proven ability to work effectively with diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications Previous classroom, clinical, laboratory, or simulation teaching experience. Experience teaching adult and/or diverse learners and assessing clinical or skills competencies. For BSN instruction, expertise in areas such as adult health, community health, psychiatric/mental health, health assessment, or other specialty areas based on program needs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Cultural Skills: Values diversity, equity, and inclusion in all aspects of work; demonstrates strong organizational skills, effective collaboration, commitment to undergraduate education, and dedication to student success. Technology Skills: Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, email, and internet tools; ability to learn organization-wide information systems, department-specific software, learning management systems, and other teaching technologies. Communication Skills: Strong oral and written communication skills with the ability to provide information, respond professionally to questions from internal and external stakeholders, and prepare routine reports and correspondence. Reasoning Ability: Ability to solve practical problems, interpret written, oral, diagram, and schedule-based instructions, work independently and collaboratively, and apply theoretical knowledge and logical reasoning as appropriate. Work Schedule and Flexibility Regular schedule: Semester-by-semester or course-based appointment. The teaching schedule may include days, evenings, and/or weekends based on course and program needs. Clinical assignments require attendance for the full scheduled clinical rotation. Hybrid eligibility: Not applicable for clinical, skills laboratory, and simulation assignments. Other instructional assignments are based on course and program needs. Physical and Work Environment Requirements Sufficient strength and mobility to work effectively with patients and students and to carry out related nursing care responsibilities, including laboratory activities. Examples include lifting and positioning up to 50 pounds, carrying up to 25 pounds, walking, medication preparation and administration, bending, and stooping. Ability to sit for extended periods while using a keyboard and to ambulate between classes and buildings on campus. Ability to be physically in attendance at the designated worksite during scheduled work hours. Normal range of vision and hearing, with or without correction. Benefits and Work-Life Highlights COMPENSATION Wage/Salary Range: BSN clinical part-time instruction: $80 per hour (clinical rotations are 126 hours). The range shown is the College's good-faith wage range for this position. The final offer will be based on relevant experience, education, skills, internal equity, and budget considerations. Application Instructions Submit the following through the Albertus Magnus College employment application portal: Cover letter Resume or curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy, if applicable The search committee or Human Resources will contact applicants selected for the first round of interviews directly. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY: Albertus Magnus College is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from qualified individuals. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
