      "title": "Position SummaryThis position directs the day-to-day operation and development of the men’s tennis program",
      "description": "Head Mens Tennis Coach - PT You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Mens Tennis Coach - PT Albertus Magnus College - NEW HAVEN, CT 06511 Apply Overview Position Type Part Time Apply Description ALBERTUS MAGNUS COLLEGE Head Men’s Tennis Coach Department Athletics Reports to Athletic Director Employment status Part-Time FLSA status Exempt Why Albertus Magnus College Founded in 1925, Albertus Magnus College has thrived through the dedication of individuals across academic and administrative roles, all committed to advancing the College’s mission and upholding the four pillars of the Dominican Tradition: Study, Prayer, Community, and Service. Today, Albertus Magnus stands as a vibrant example of modern higher education. Position Summary This position directs the day-to-day operation and development of the men’s tennis program at Albertus Magnus College. The Head Coach is accountable for building and maintaining the requisite roster sizes and developing a student-athlete recruitment plan to ensure the long-term sustainability of an appropriate roster. The coach implements a strength and conditioning program and manages all practices and games. The position is also responsible for the supervision of assistant coaches. Qualifications Essential Duties and Responsibilities Develops and implements a recruiting plan to achieve and maintain a roster size adequate for sponsorship of men’s tennis in accordance with the College’s enrollment growth strategies. Develops and implements a daily practice plan to insure proper preparation for intercollegiate competition. In conjunction with the Director of Athletics, works with local facilities and/or municipalities to coordinate practice and/or competition. Provides contest preparation by scouting opponents. Promotes the visions and values of Albertus Magnus College by emphasizing the experience and education of each student-athlete as the most important component of intercollegiate athletic participation. Supervises assistant coaches and provides feedback for continued growth and development. Provides a year-round strength and conditioning program tailored towards the individual sport. Represents their program during coaches’ meetings. Coordinates fundraising activities to benefit the student-athlete experience for the men’s tennis program Required Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required. Current safety certifications (CPR /First Aid, a valid driver’s license) are required, or an ability to obtain Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Outstanding verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience as a student-athlete or coach of the sport. Knowledge of NCAA Division III rules and regulations, including compliance. A demonstrated commitment to the NCAA Division III philosophy regarding the student-athlete experience Work Schedule and Flexibility Evening and some weekend hours required Physical and Work Environment Requirements Compensation The total compensation for the Part-Time Head Men’s Tennis Coach position is $6,000 for the academic year. This amount will be divided into equal monthly payments and paid on the last business day of each month. Application Instructions Submit the following through [application portal/link]: Cover letter Resume or curriculum vitae 3 Professional references [Statement of teaching philosophy, if applicable] Applicants selected for the first round of interviews will be contacted directly by the search committee or Human Resources. Albertus Magnus College is an equal-opportunity employer and invites all qualified applicants to consider this opportunity and apply. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
